# DEAD FRAGMENT — kept, read by nothing.
#
# Twenty lines of nginx `location /cams/…` blocks that proxy an MJPEG stream and a still frame per camera
# to rtsp.int.leighhack.org, from the vhost that served the camera wall.  Nothing in this repo
# reads this file: no `import`, no `include`, and no such `location` in any rendered config
# (measured 2026-10-22: `grep -rn "streams\|/cams/" machines/services1` finds only this file and no
# vhost, and `rtsp.int` is in neither `common/int-dns.nix` nor `common/dns-records.nix`).

# It used to sit at `machines/services1/streams.ignore`, which was worse in every way: `*.ignore`
# is git-ignored, so the flake cannot see it and neither can `git status`, while its contents
# looked exactly like config that was live — the precise trap AGENTS.md rule 5 exists for.  If
# the camera wall comes back, this is the shape it had; wire it through a real module.

# The fragment itself, follows:

# Streams
# location /cams/3d1 {
#     proxy_pass https://rtsp.int.leighhack.org/api/stream.mjpeg?src=3d_1;
# }
# location /cams/3d2 {
#     proxy_pass https://rtsp.int.leighhack.org/api/stream.mjpeg?src=3d_2;
# }
# location /cams/3d3 {
#     proxy_pass https://rtsp.int.leighhack.org/api/stream.mjpeg?src=3d_3;
# }
# location /cams/cnc {
#     proxy_pass https://rtsp.int.leighhack.org/api/stream.mjpeg?src=cnc;
# }

# Error image for cameras
# location = /error.jpg {
#     root /var/www/html;
# }

# Statics
# location /cams/3d1.jpg {
#     proxy_pass https://rtsp.int.leighhack.org/api/frame.jpeg?src=3d_1;
#     proxy_connect_timeout 5;
#     proxy_read_timeout 5;
#     proxy_send_timeout 5;
#     error_page 504 /error.jpg;
# }
# location /cams/3d2.jpg {
#     proxy_pass https://rtsp.int.leighhack.org/api/frame.jpeg?src=3d_2;
#     proxy_connect_timeout 5;
#     proxy_read_timeout 5;
#     proxy_send_timeout 5;
#     error_page 504 /error.jpg;
# }
